        "teacherMoves": "'For the last 8 minutes build your own model on a fresh page. Draw the nested Venn diagram big enough to write in, label all five regions with their names and symbols, and place four cards. You MUST include π and one sentence connecting it to the sufuria.' Circulate and initial correctly structured models. If π is in the wrong region, ask quietly: 'Can π be written as p over q with integers? Look at 87.96459430…; what do you notice about the digits?' Wait 10 seconds before more help. With 2 minutes left: 'Write the title. Do not close this page; we will add to it in every lesson.' Collect books whose models you have not initialled.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative individual model building: a personal model at the end of each lesson gives learners a visual record of growing understanding. Requiring π in the model every time keeps the sufuria phenomenon at the centre of each revision.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Observable indicators: (1) the nested structure is correct (ℕ inside ℤ inside ℚ inside ℝ, with irrationals in ℝ but not ℚ); a flat diagram means the subset idea has not yet landed; (2) π is in the irrational region with a justification that mentions 'cannot write as p/q' or 'never ends or repeats'; (3) every card placed is correct. Initial 8 to 10 models in class and review the rest after class."
