      "purposeInStoryline": "In Lesson 1 learners were introduced to the Ugali Pot Problem and confronted the puzzle that 28 × π produces a never-ending, non-repeating decimal. In Lesson 2 learners sorted 12 Kenyan numbers into the nested real number system (natural numbers, integers, rational and irrational numbers inside the real numbers). Lesson 3 now gives learners the formal classification tools to answer the puzzle directly: they investigate the decimal structure of many everyday numbers — unga prices, distances, square roots of areas — and discover that most are rational (their decimals stop or repeat), while π and √2 are provably irrational. By the end of this lesson learners can explain precisely why the sufuria circumference can never be written as an exact fraction, advancing the driving question significantly.",
