        "teacherMoves": "'You are decimal detectives: look carefully at what the calculator shows and describe it, like a scientist recording an observation.' Allow 6 minutes. Visit pairs who think 22/7 = π: 'Enter 22 ÷ 7, then π. Are the digits after 3.14 identical?' Wait 10 seconds. Project the two displays and ask: 'A Nairobi architect and a mama mboga both use 22/7 for π. Is 22/7 actually equal to π?' Wait 10 seconds and cold-call 2 learners. Say: 'Write the key difference in red; it is the most important observation today.' Cold-call 2 pairs for their sentence and record key phrases on the board.",
