        "teacherMoves": "'In 12 minutes do three things: fill the table to 4 decimal places, agree a reason for each card, and peg it.' Assign roles: Calculator Operator, Peg Placer, Justification Writer and Kericho Temperature Analyst. Circulate and ask one targeted question per group without answering placement questions: 'You placed π − 3 there; what did your calculator give? Between which two numbers is that?' and 'Is √3 bigger or smaller than 1.5? How do you know?' At the 10-minute mark ask the Analysts: 'Which temperatures are irrational? What makes you say so?' Ring a bell at 12 minutes: 'Step back and look at the whole class line. Do all groups agree where 2.333… sits?'",
