        "teacherMoves": "'Some cards may be in the wrong place. In our Mathematical Court each group defends one card and the court decides: keep or move, and why.' Assign √2, π − 3, −√3 and 2.333…. After each defence ask: 'Decimal? Between which two numbers? Justification?' Wait 10 seconds, then take 2 challengers from different groups. For irrationals press: 'You said √2 ≈ 1.4142. Can you write it exactly? How do you KNOW it belongs there and not a millimetre to the right?' Wait 15 seconds; this is the key productive struggle. Then ask the sufuria question and cold-call 2 learners; confirm that the gap is real, matters in engineering and cooking, and is why approximation exists.",
